{
  "id": "sketch-v1",
  "description": "default-v1 with the budgets cut and the print pass removed, used only for the three sketches per problem in the artist loop. A sketch is a question about composition, not a finished plate: it has a fifth of the marks, a third of the nodes, four text ops instead of twelve, and no print stages, so a sketch costs a fraction of a render and can never be mistaken for a final piece. Nothing in this profile widens anything -- every limit is at or below default-v1, so a program that is legal here is legal there.",
